' FactStamp — Data Flow Diagram, Level 1
' Tool: PlantUML   Build: plantuml -tsvg dfd_level_1.puml
' Decomposes process "0 FactStamp System" from the Level 0 context diagram
' into processes 1.0 - 8.0 and the six Firestore collections D1 - D6.
' NOTE: there is deliberately NO "Verifications" data store — verifications are
' an embedded array field on each claim document in D1 Claims.
' 8.0 Award Reputation is the awardVerificationReputation Cloud Function
' (functions/index.js), the automatic, verification-driven writer of
' users.reputation / totalVerifications. Ordinary clients cannot write those
' fields (firestore.rules); an administrator can override them through 7.0.
' 4.0 runs in the browser and only reads reputation; it never writes D2.
' D3 Notifications is server-written: 8.0 emits claim_verified,
' verdict_submitted and reputation_update notifications for the verifiers and
' claim author, while 7.0 broadcasts weekly-report / system messages.
'
' Rule 2 (Diagram-rules.md): PlantUML has no native DFD notation, so DFD shapes
' are mapped onto the nearest PlantUML constructs:
'   process        -> usecase  (ellipse / bubble)
'   data store     -> database (cylinder)
'   external entity-> rectangle (box)
' Rule 5: no "left to right direction" — A4 portrait, reads top-to-bottom.
'
' SIMPLIFIED: opposite flows between the same pair of nodes are drawn as one
' two-headed arrow (<-->), and minor read-backs are folded into them, which cuts
' the diagram to 24 flows.
'   -[hidden]->  = invisible spine edge (pins a node to the rank below its peer)
'   -[norank]->  = a flow that must not stretch the vertical spine
@startuml
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultFontName "Liberation Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam defaultFontStyle bold
skinparam titleFontSize 26
skinparam titleFontStyle bold

' Rule 5 (portrait): stretch ranks apart, squeeze columns together.
skinparam ranksep 110
skinparam nodesep 15

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ArrowThickness 2.5
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ArrowFontStyle bold

skinparam UsecaseBorderColor black
skinparam UsecaseBorderThickness 2.5
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam UsecaseFontSize 19
skinparam UsecaseFontStyle bold

skinparam RectangleBorderColor black
skinparam RectangleBorderThickness 2.5
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam RectangleFontSize 20
skinparam RectangleFontStyle bold

skinparam DatabaseBorderColor black
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam DatabaseFontSize 19
skinparam DatabaseFontStyle bold

title FactStamp - Data Flow Diagram (Level 1)

' ---------- Nodes, declared top to bottom ----------
rectangle "Registered\nVerifier" as VER
usecase "Submit Claim" as P1
usecase "Detect Duplicates" as P2
database "Claims\n(verifications[])" as D1
database "Claim Media" as D6
usecase "Manage\nVerification Queue" as P3
usecase "Compute Weighted\nConsensus" as P4
database "Users" as D2
usecase "Award Reputation\n(Cloud Function)" as P8
database "Notifications" as D3
usecase "Produce Analytics" as P6
usecase "Generate\nFact-Check Card" as P5
rectangle "Visitor\n(Read-Only)" as VIS
usecase "Administer\n& Audit" as P7
database "Reports" as D4
database "Audit Logs" as D5
rectangle "Administrator" as ADM

' ---------- Spine ----------
D1  -[hidden]right- D6
D2  -[hidden]right- P4
P4  -[hidden]down- P5
P4  -[hidden]down- P6
VIS -[hidden]down- P7

' ---------- 1.0 and 2.0: submission ----------
P1 <-right-> VER : "Claim /\nReceipt or\nDuplicate Warning"
P1  <--> P2 : "Normalised Text /\nDuplicate Match"
P1  --> D1 : "New Claim"
P1  --> D6 : "Full Screenshot"
D1  -left-> P2 : "Claim\nCorpus"

' ---------- 3.0 and 4.0: verification and consensus ----------
VER --> P3 : "Verdict +\nSource URL"
D1  <--> P3 : "Pending Queue /\nNew Verification"
D6  --> P3 : "Screenshot"
P3  --> P4 : "Quorum Reached\n(3 Verifications)"
D2  -[norank]-> P4 : "Verifier\nReputation"
D1 <-- P4 : "Verdict +\nConfidence"
VER <-- D3 : "Verdict\nNotification"

' ---------- 8.0: server-side reputation (Admin SDK trigger on claims/{claimId}) ----------
D1  --> P8 : "Appended Verification /\nSettled Verdict"
P8  --> D2 : "Reputation +\nVerification Count"
P8  --> D3 : "Consensus / Verdict /\nReputation Notifications"

' ---------- 5.0 and 6.0: public outputs ----------
D1  --> P5 : "Settled Claim"
D1  --> P6 : "Claim Statistics"
P5  --> VIS : "Fact-Check\nCard (PNG)"
P6  --> VIS : "Analytics\nDashboard"

' ---------- 7.0: administration ----------
ADM <-up-> P7 : "Moderation Action /\nAudit Trail"
P7  <--> D4 : "Incident\nReports"
P7  --> D5 : "Audit Entry"
P7  --> D3 : "Weekly Report /\nSystem Broadcast"
D1 <-- P7 : "Override /\nFlag / Expiry"
D2 <-[norank]- P7 : "Reputation /\nRole Override"
@enduml
